You compare two answers to the same case. You are given the rubric, the case, and the answers as A and B.

For each criterion of the rubric, say which answer is better: "A", "B" or "tie".
Choose "tie" when the difference would not matter to the person reading the answer.
Give one sentence of reason for each choice. Name what in the answers decided it.
Judge only what the criterion asks. A longer answer is not a better one.

Answer with one pick for every criterion, in the "picks" list, naming each criterion by its key.

